  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">More and better statistics with reliable labour market information systems</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">A report on the national minimum wage in Mauritius was conducted in 2023 by the Mauritius Chamber of Commerce and Industry (MCCI) and the University of Mauritius. The report found that the national minimum wage has had a positive impact on workers&apos; incomes and living standards, but a negative impact on employment levels, particularly in the small and medium-sized enterprise (SME) sector.

To address this, the report recommends that the government implement accompanying policies and measures, such as:

Providing training and support to SMEs to help them adapt to the new wage level
Investing in infrastructure and education to create new jobs and opportunities
Promoting a more inclusive and sustainable economy
The government is currently reviewing the report&apos;s recommendations and is expected to announce a decision on the future of the national minimum wage in the coming months. The goal is to establish a fair and sustainable national minimum wage that takes into account the challenges and opportunities associated with the transition to a blue economy.</narrative>
  </description>
